Observation:
- Lowering random_page_cost makes index-based access more attractive
  to the planner.
- Planner decision changed even though data and query were identical.
- Execution time improved significantly with lower random_page_cost.

Conclusion:
- random_page_cost strongly influences PostgreSQL planner behavior.
- Cost parameters should reflect actual storage characteristics.
- Incorrect cost assumptions can lead to suboptimal plans.
